Purpose
The goal of this document is to describe how to administrate Fabric and Power BI through it.

Glossary

Microsoft 365

Cloud-based productivity, collaboration, identity, security, and administration ecosystem. Microsoft 365 is structured around a tenant, which represents the organization’s cloud environment. Users, groups, subscriptions, licenses, domains, applications, policies, and administrative roles are associated with this tenant. Microsoft 365 administration is based on roles. Instead of giving every administrator unrestricted control, organizations can assign roles that correspond to particular responsibilities, such as user management, license management, billing, service support, security, or application administration.

Fabric

Microsoft Fabric is Microsoft’s end-to-end, software-as-a-service analytics platform. It integrates data ingestion, data transformation, data engineering, data science, data warehousing, real-time intelligence, databases, business intelligence, and reporting within a common environment. Fabric uses organizational accounts and groups maintained in Microsoft Entra ID. User and administrative access is therefore connected to the organization’s Microsoft cloud identity environment. The Fabric Administrator role provides access to organization-wide Fabric administration capabilities without requiring the account to have unrestricted Microsoft 365 Global Administrator privileges.

Power BI

Power BI is Microsoft’s business analytics and business-intelligence platform. It enables users to connect to data, create semantic models, develop interactive reports and dashboards, analyze information, and securely share insights across an organization. A Power BI Administration Account is an organizational Microsoft Entra user account authorized to perform tenant-level administration for the Power BI service. In the current unified administration model, these responsibilities are commonly performed through the Fabric Administrator role or, in some organizational configurations, the Power Platform Administrator role. Power BI administration is therefore closely integrated with Fabric administration.

